[{:db/id "q-353186/field-1/1ca61f911376672717029869ec78407128ca8e513032fbc49dfe9e243b9392ff" :answer/id #uuid "9677a68b-ce2c-5b3a-a2fc-2e2c91a81ef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4803" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353186/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5666ae7b-ae88-54f7-9bf7-f1ea2f2950fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353186/field-1/1ca61f911376672717029869ec78407128ca8e513032fbc49dfe9e243b9392ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-353186/field-1/1ca61f911376672717029869ec78407128ca8e513032fbc49dfe9e243b9392ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353186" :question/id #uuid "8654a467-e62f-57bb-93c7-57b0d02f8c50" :question/math-academy-id "q-353186" :question/problem "The number of cells in a petri dish $C(t)$ after $t$ hours can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=C.\n$$\n\nIf there are currently $650$ cells in the petri dish, calculate the number of cells after $2$ hours. Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nThe number of cells after $2$ hours is approximately \n{{field-1}}\ncells." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of cells using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=C.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nC(t)={C}_{0}\\,{e}^{t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $650$ cells in the petri dish, so we have ${C}_{0}=650.$\n\nTherefore, the number of cells $C$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nC(t)=650\\,{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of cells when $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(2) & =650\\,{e}^{2} \\\\  & ≈4802.89\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the number of cells after $2$ hours is approximately $4803$ cells." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353186/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ba25c0c-9ba9-586a-b66f-7f07076d2827"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353186"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83144/selection/465ef01d86d37637cc9db1d2b3a4299669a4b6350ae84494b27874168165e228" :answer/id #uuid "1b6274f1-d015-56f4-9224-742484bafa2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27\\,332" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83144/selection/4a5db5460effe4170eff073577d81804ebb0ed294d624f6eeda27590844181cb" :answer/id #uuid "b307080c-712f-54e2-be70-6e9ea3d7cc2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22\\,377" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83144/selection/d0d27503ee624c3e8f6074ad8aaad7e8850833c6ccd0b9a99e0571ed2bf96a5f" :answer/id #uuid "d2cb9fc9-2541-533d-b278-2db09abb03d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31\\,755" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83144/selection/a6b3d9c589a1f61d3f71134b03d816f7b59de6e36e52207b18445684dadfc5d0" :answer/id #uuid "e41987f4-94a9-50a0-83b0-9e8eb978238c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,248" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83144/selection/1269238e825ab502eda5573fb9c9aac2dd2f753ad9896273ef9a196bb9c2c7f9" :answer/id #uuid "9af93ca2-f624-5d72-899e-d7ccdd0e6168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,731" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83144/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4df97d5d-d1f0-547c-81a9-3414beafde79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83144/selection/465ef01d86d37637cc9db1d2b3a4299669a4b6350ae84494b27874168165e228" :answer-field/choices ["q-83144/selection/465ef01d86d37637cc9db1d2b3a4299669a4b6350ae84494b27874168165e228" "q-83144/selection/4a5db5460effe4170eff073577d81804ebb0ed294d624f6eeda27590844181cb" "q-83144/selection/d0d27503ee624c3e8f6074ad8aaad7e8850833c6ccd0b9a99e0571ed2bf96a5f" "q-83144/selection/a6b3d9c589a1f61d3f71134b03d816f7b59de6e36e52207b18445684dadfc5d0" "q-83144/selection/1269238e825ab502eda5573fb9c9aac2dd2f753ad9896273ef9a196bb9c2c7f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83144" :question/id #uuid "c60fbb60-b78a-5c24-90ef-165c91d4dd65" :question/math-academy-id "q-83144" :question/problem "The number of subscribers $S(t)$ to a video channel after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0.05S.\n$$\n\nIf the channel currently has $15\\,000$ subscribers, calculate the number of subscribers after $12$ weeks. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of subscribers using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0.05S.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nS(t)={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.05t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that the channel currently has $15\\,000$ subscribers, so we have ${S}_{0}=15\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the number of subscribers $S$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nS(t)=15\\,000\\,{e}^{0.05t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of subscribers when $t=12,$ we substitute $t=12$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(12) & =15\\,000\\,{e}^{0.05\\cdot 12} \\\\  & =15\\,000\\,{e}^{0.6} \\\\  & ≈27\\,331.78\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the number of subscribers is $27\\,332$ after $12$ weeks." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83144/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ba25c0c-9ba9-586a-b66f-7f07076d2827"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119231/selection/5cabf25d07382504e95a770b2191a943e2e242b93d0fdc9a748721dfff5953f7" :answer/id #uuid "ba740ff2-5a93-5217-a330-7d9123b718ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,981" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119231/selection/db1af0f4562be74ecc867fbb03d09dea8256728e8a66e5d22c592dd16a505207" :answer/id #uuid "90e605a5-9568-5dd0-bbef-c12cb7840fd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11\\,052" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119231/selection/7b3121dfba2cea438993e33f3ea5c87696199fdcfeba3777d126d66afde9b090" :answer/id #uuid "49ec0a8b-005f-53dc-a28e-ed3000e58c89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,231" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119231/selection/67c4e0002a0b02d2e07c552a500e4bfd614f5c4d5acde1f6acd69b31e956e237" :answer/id #uuid "39f63ed7-ab7d-53a9-b263-ed5407f6b26f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13\\,002" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119231/selection/3a7f051f47147d3fc61426e0aa851f95a816e1d605dc95bc08c8f49d6cf97daf" :answer/id #uuid "70ed1f03-582d-52f4-bea5-294909e97b01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,564" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119231/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f4ac8bb-fa3b-5ae2-9aa7-46f343f9a358" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119231/selection/db1af0f4562be74ecc867fbb03d09dea8256728e8a66e5d22c592dd16a505207" :answer-field/choices ["q-119231/selection/5cabf25d07382504e95a770b2191a943e2e242b93d0fdc9a748721dfff5953f7" "q-119231/selection/db1af0f4562be74ecc867fbb03d09dea8256728e8a66e5d22c592dd16a505207" "q-119231/selection/7b3121dfba2cea438993e33f3ea5c87696199fdcfeba3777d126d66afde9b090" "q-119231/selection/67c4e0002a0b02d2e07c552a500e4bfd614f5c4d5acde1f6acd69b31e956e237" "q-119231/selection/3a7f051f47147d3fc61426e0aa851f95a816e1d605dc95bc08c8f49d6cf97daf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119231" :question/id #uuid "c40bcda7-b5a6-51e6-b219-ea1070a93d2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-119231" :question/problem "The number of subscribers $S(t)$ to a certain site's e-mail news service after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0.01S.\n$$\n\nIf the site's e-mail news service currently has $10\\,000$ subscribers, calculate the number of subscribers after $10$ weeks. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of subscribers using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0.01S.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nS(t)={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.01t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that the service currently has $10\\,000$ subscribers, so we have ${S}_{0}=10\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the number of subscribers $S$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nS(t)=10\\,000\\,{e}^{0.01t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of subscribers when $t=10,$ we substitute $t=10$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(10) & =10\\,000\\,{e}^{0.01\\cdot 10} \\\\  & =10\\,000\\,{e}^{0.1} \\\\  & ≈11\\,051.71\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the number of subscribers is $11\\,052$ after $10$ weeks." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119231/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ba25c0c-9ba9-586a-b66f-7f07076d2827"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119231"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353180/field-1/d9e921519175a8a61bd3ca57a54fff6403f2577d6c9e998ae8d19efbc858697c" :answer/id #uuid "9add05ac-23bf-5d46-ae06-db4cf2e4006e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "612" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353180/field-1/5dadf689b856c9606d336ca6f3a1d51fb0d2d10248451cfef53b1b1936486035" :answer/id #uuid "3fed065a-493c-5148-b976-2da758676fa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "527" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353180/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c6d1fee-ef19-5fa6-8251-8d71b5171c48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353180/field-1/d9e921519175a8a61bd3ca57a54fff6403f2577d6c9e998ae8d19efbc858697c" :answer-field/choices ["q-353180/field-1/d9e921519175a8a61bd3ca57a54fff6403f2577d6c9e998ae8d19efbc858697c" "q-353180/field-1/5dadf689b856c9606d336ca6f3a1d51fb0d2d10248451cfef53b1b1936486035"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353180" :question/id #uuid "dc57d4c3-f9ce-5dc5-b93e-82a6951acb1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-353180" :question/problem "The amount of a rare plant species $A(t)$ after $t$ years can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.072A.\n$$\n\nIf there are currently $320$ plants, calculate the amount after $9$ years. Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nThe amount of the plant species after $9$ years is approximately \n{{field-1}}\nplants." :question/worked-solution "We model the amount using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.072A.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nA(t)={A}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.072t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${A}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $320$ plants, so we have ${A}_{0}=320.$\n\nTherefore, the amount $A$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nA(t)=320\\,{e}^{0.072t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the amount when $t=9,$ we substitute $t=9$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(9) & =320\\,{e}^{0.072\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =320\\,{e}^{0.648} \\\\  & ≈611.53\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the amount of the plant species after $9$ years is approximately $612$ plants." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353180/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ba25c0c-9ba9-586a-b66f-7f07076d2827"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353180"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353189/field-1/704810f5c82844e1ff49f0f639e05cd66bd09fe61a0bf3875394a6628487b079" :answer/id #uuid "8172599c-825e-576a-8ea4-08060102d028" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6552" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353189/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9189fc2a-319c-5b02-a1f4-4ce9a7148e01" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353189/field-1/704810f5c82844e1ff49f0f639e05cd66bd09fe61a0bf3875394a6628487b079" :answer-field/choices ["q-353189/field-1/704810f5c82844e1ff49f0f639e05cd66bd09fe61a0bf3875394a6628487b079"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353189" :question/id #uuid "feef296b-d2d1-5b32-88ba-3108b3f1a18d" :question/math-academy-id "q-353189" :question/problem "The number of insects in a controlled habitat $H(t)$ after $t$ months can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=2H.\n$$\n\nIf there are currently $120$ insects in the habitat, calculate the number of insects after $2$ months. Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nThe number of insects after $2$ months is approximately \n{{field-1}}\ninsects." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of insects using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=2H.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nH(t)={H}_{0}\\,{e}^{2t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${H}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $120$ insects in the habitat, so we have ${H}_{0}=120.$\n\nTherefore, the number of insects $H$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nH(t)=120\\,{e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of insects when $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H(2) & =120\\,{e}^{2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =120\\,{e}^{4} \\\\  & ≈6551.78\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the number of insects after $2$ months is approximately $6552$ insects." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353189/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ba25c0c-9ba9-586a-b66f-7f07076d2827"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353189"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119341/selection/bd9c0fdc1cb3a8f2801d56adcbe073e1fe7c0f94cbaf3865bf892ce4ad850c33" :answer/id #uuid "656f9fa0-8c9c-5ecf-a867-a7e8aff11624" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36\\,788" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119341/selection/4d5d6be21d16de50c12e3269fb186dfeb23d6b28a23e06fc513a909ea3ff6894" :answer/id #uuid "b28c122f-1012-5fef-adc9-c9a80afa4efb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42\\,125" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119341/selection/ae147e59a8f5ad5f8c9c225d7a69b3fe057ffe75614775ec46672d0c5540d54d" :answer/id #uuid "54853199-f168-53ba-a585-689664f50bf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "67\\,124" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119341/selection/1b4606f7f4d6c22dfa6fcf4359755061185a23fe26b7a7f90d9e792e9fa90cda" :answer/id #uuid "f347ea5a-346a-5114-a80f-82a5223d3312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "73\\,558" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119341/selection/199ee31ee104fc0221c6c3bdb5624f0a0098c3e8387b437d8f62c22ba1e5abc2" :answer/id #uuid "c47ea5a8-edf2-52fd-87f7-826960587250" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52\\,009" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119341/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f14decb-5086-55da-8c82-9a07ed193f9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119341/selection/bd9c0fdc1cb3a8f2801d56adcbe073e1fe7c0f94cbaf3865bf892ce4ad850c33" :answer-field/choices ["q-119341/selection/bd9c0fdc1cb3a8f2801d56adcbe073e1fe7c0f94cbaf3865bf892ce4ad850c33" "q-119341/selection/4d5d6be21d16de50c12e3269fb186dfeb23d6b28a23e06fc513a909ea3ff6894" "q-119341/selection/ae147e59a8f5ad5f8c9c225d7a69b3fe057ffe75614775ec46672d0c5540d54d" "q-119341/selection/1b4606f7f4d6c22dfa6fcf4359755061185a23fe26b7a7f90d9e792e9fa90cda" "q-119341/selection/199ee31ee104fc0221c6c3bdb5624f0a0098c3e8387b437d8f62c22ba1e5abc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119341" :question/id #uuid "a23ea5e1-0ee0-52e5-9a48-03228f9f384c" :question/math-academy-id "q-119341" :question/problem "The number of sales $S(t)$ of a new tech device $t$ weeks after the start of sales can be modeled by the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-0.1S.\n$$\n\nIf there were $100\\,000$ sales initially, calculate the number of sales after $10$ weeks. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of sales using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-0.1S.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nS(t)={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.1t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there were $100\\,000$  sales initially, so we have ${S}_{0}=100\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the number of sales $S$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nS(t)=100\\,000\\,{e}^{-0.1t}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of sales when $t=10,$ we substitute $t=10$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(10) & =100\\,000\\,{e}^{-0.1\\cdot 10} \\\\  & =100\\,000\\,{e}^{-1} \\\\  & ≈36\\,787.94\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that there are $36\\,788$ sales after $10$ weeks." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119341/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6330530-50c5-51e9-b616-2b97ce42cade"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119341"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353197/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6e70b314-7cb4-50fc-9cef-8081bc5c1703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353197/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6403680c-f1a9-5852-bc72-d5f361921597" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353197/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3bfd94-f0c9-586b-86e9-42f31a464767" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353197/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-353197/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-353197/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353197" :question/id #uuid "4bd3a121-3322-5ea9-bdc3-c2499562a25c" :question/math-academy-id "q-353197" :question/problem "The population of a bacterial culture $P(t)$ after $t$ hours can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-P.\n$$\n\nIf there are currently $30$ bacteria in the culture, calculate the population after $3$ hours. Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nThe population after $3$ hours is approximately \n{{field-1}}\nbacteria." :question/worked-solution "We model the population using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-P.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{-t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $30$ bacteria in the culture, so we have ${P}_{0}=30.$\n\nTherefore, the population $P$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nP(t)=30\\,{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the population when $t=3,$ we substitute $t=3$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3) & =30\\,{e}^{-1\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =30\\,{e}^{-3} \\\\  & ≈1.49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the population after $3$ hours is approximately $1$ bacterium." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353197/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6330530-50c5-51e9-b616-2b97ce42cade"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353197"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186088358 :question/answer-fields 17592186087078] {:db/id "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/d86492ad3364ea24aa0aa1a846deb1b49f18d5922155f7a267a4de7b2b8d03bb" :answer/id #uuid "28ef58b4-ec49-5e98-842b-7bbbc5f2cd1e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$125$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/beedb48d18c95ec5cd811dfc04efab9670c2c74f7b4b6d1b276a52b267ad6321" :answer/id #uuid "f6e5e585-db2d-57a6-996a-eaabc38b092a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$586$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/67b8880449ed227a57bdbbc0e019b279ffd5eb8831ceb0254f156c4a9b51b909" :answer/id #uuid "9a183988-6145-5d00-861e-8bf742aaaac5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$216$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/2065e25468d361d6315f56f488fac1873a63b6d5b7fcb3f95cbe4985c75044e8" :answer/id #uuid "6e35f9a8-8574-5dac-82f0-64e2238983fc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$355$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/b7244870186530318c54a4a0ccf46afd4bde825c62c59ce02d8c818a85f63453" :answer/id #uuid "42824b19-4e9b-583a-afe4-e945c4b2d9ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$966$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660" :answer-field/id #uuid "8908f557-6255-566a-9d74-9fa5f6444d55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/beedb48d18c95ec5cd811dfc04efab9670c2c74f7b4b6d1b276a52b267ad6321" :answer-field/choices ["q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/d86492ad3364ea24aa0aa1a846deb1b49f18d5922155f7a267a4de7b2b8d03bb" "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/beedb48d18c95ec5cd811dfc04efab9670c2c74f7b4b6d1b276a52b267ad6321" "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/67b8880449ed227a57bdbbc0e019b279ffd5eb8831ceb0254f156c4a9b51b909" "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/2065e25468d361d6315f56f488fac1873a63b6d5b7fcb3f95cbe4985c75044e8" "q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660/b7244870186530318c54a4a0ccf46afd4bde825c62c59ce02d8c818a85f63453"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-83140"] :question/problem "The outstanding amount $L(t)$ that Daphne needs to repay the bank $t$ years after taking out a loan can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}=-0.5L.\n$$\n\nIf she borrowed $$32\\,000,$ calculate the debt remaining after $8$ years. Round your answer to the nearest dollar." :question/worked-solution "We model the amount of debt remaining using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}=-0.5L.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nL(t)={L}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.5t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${L}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that $$32\\,000$ were borrowed, so we have ${L}_{0}=32\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the amount of debt $L$ remaining at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nL(t)=32\\,000\\,{e}^{-0.5t}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the amount of debt remaining when $t=8,$ we substitute $t=8$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(8) & =32\\,000\\,{e}^{-0.5\\cdot 8} \\\\  & =32\\,000\\,{e}^{-4} \\\\  & ≈586.100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that $586$ dollars of debt remain." :question/answer-fields ["q-83140/selection/ma-v1/132f48b0664773c91ddac47dea24892515c23f0fe86a14def135296b1c95d660"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-15208"] :question/problem "The number of particles $N(t)$ in a radioactive substance after $t$ years can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-3N.\n$$\n\nIf there were $8\\,500$ particles initially, calculate the number of particles remaining after $2$ years. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of particles in the substance using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-3N.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nN(t)={N}_{0}\\,{e}^{-3t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${N}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there were $8\\,500$ particles initially, so we have ${N}_{0}=8\\,500.$\n\nTherefore, the number of particles $N$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nN(t)=8\\,500\\,{e}^{-3t}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of particles when $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(2) & =8\\,500\\,{e}^{-3\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =8\\,500\\,{e}^{-6} \\\\  & ≈21.069\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that $21$ particles remain." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339591/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "2e18578c-8078-52a9-b2fa-92741c2b9a7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339591/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "765bccbb-f980-5aea-9419-5bc25597f852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339591/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "7b105f8c-9e15-5ae9-9e85-a3c149ee6050" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339591/selection/0b264a929df91f183c31537acf560edd2114ab983879cbe61ea3aed58b55bda9" :answer/id #uuid "8c8e3b9f-d69f-553e-a266-acd230f66bf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339591/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "ee491660-d139-5093-ab7d-71e48a593422" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339591/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d66d1a32-dcab-504b-96f8-a85df87b3592" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339591/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer-field/choices ["q-339591/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" "q-339591/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" "q-339591/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-339591/selection/0b264a929df91f183c31537acf560edd2114ab983879cbe61ea3aed58b55bda9" "q-339591/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339591" :question/id #uuid "dc797367-c6c0-52d2-9b58-712548881bd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-339591" :question/problem "The mass of a radioactive sample $R(t)$ (in milligrams) after $t$ days can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=-0.05R.\n$$\n\nIf the sample initially had a mass of $80$ milligrams, calculate its mass after $30$ days. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We model the mass of the sample using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=-0.05R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nR(t)={R}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.05t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${R}_{0}$ is the initial mass.\n\nWe're told that the initial mass of the sample is $80$ milligrams, so we have ${R}_{0}=80.$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the sample $R$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nR(t)=80\\,{e}^{-0.05t}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the mass of the sample when $t=30,$ we substitute $t=30$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(30) & =80\\,{e}^{-0.05\\cdot 30} \\\\  & =80\\,{e}^{-1.5} \\\\  & =17.850…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the mass of the sample after $30$ days is $18$ milligrams." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339591/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6330530-50c5-51e9-b616-2b97ce42cade"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339651/selection/c036e9b91f083d0c01fd5027e3573e656fa3351c5342373013af13310b80868c" :answer/id #uuid "abf4d2fc-a1d3-56cc-b06d-3cf1ac8c1c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339651/selection/3928339a7ca3734c5192ffd97da4f8004ce35965f00d00aa3e42516cd2f378a2" :answer/id #uuid "99dec1fb-0bcd-59ea-83ad-f427c918441e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339651/selection/de4b22bb2386e6d61bcf3f2723fe11db6770ef34ce47348312c93d2cfefa4f56" :answer/id #uuid "a7513e07-8013-5bcc-809b-361222c97578" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339651/selection/a1cb8f30c60ee00c48b878a83ec3ad994990968dc2b928bacb24797eb1b8bc42" :answer/id #uuid "b5e7e894-55df-5f7c-8287-8e131c62152f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339651/selection/4a70b363dc4d15ca8c68b143dbb028ea0583f45e8f0dceeb6e61615cc8c69071" :answer/id #uuid "d44d8070-6ed2-54f0-b953-74962fcef638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339651/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6118ae18-c606-5e01-9621-e4392e9d3275" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339651/selection/de4b22bb2386e6d61bcf3f2723fe11db6770ef34ce47348312c93d2cfefa4f56" :answer-field/choices ["q-339651/selection/c036e9b91f083d0c01fd5027e3573e656fa3351c5342373013af13310b80868c" "q-339651/selection/3928339a7ca3734c5192ffd97da4f8004ce35965f00d00aa3e42516cd2f378a2" "q-339651/selection/de4b22bb2386e6d61bcf3f2723fe11db6770ef34ce47348312c93d2cfefa4f56" "q-339651/selection/a1cb8f30c60ee00c48b878a83ec3ad994990968dc2b928bacb24797eb1b8bc42" "q-339651/selection/4a70b363dc4d15ca8c68b143dbb028ea0583f45e8f0dceeb6e61615cc8c69071"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339651" :question/id #uuid "121b5edf-571a-5e51-9959-cd353a83487b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339651" :question/problem "The value of a savings account $A=A(t)$ after $t$ years can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA,\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is the growth rate. If the account initially had $$12\\,000,$ and $A(4)=$15\\,000,$ calculate the growth rate $k$ to the nearest percent." :question/worked-solution "We model the value of the savings account using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nA(t)={A}_{0}\\,{e}^{kt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${A}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that the account initially had $$12\\,000,$ so we have ${A}_{0}=12\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the value $A$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nA(t)=12\\,000\\,{e}^{kt}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $k,$ we substitute $A(4)=15\\,000$ into the equation above and solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(4) & =12\\,000\\,{e}^{k\\cdot 4} \\\\ 15\\,000 & =12\\,000\\,{e}^{4k} \\\\ {e}^{4k} & =\\frac{15\\,000}{12\\,000} \\\\ {e}^{4k} & =1.25 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4k}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.25) \\\\ 4k & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.25) \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.25) \\\\ k & =0.055\\,78…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k≈6%,$ rounded to the nearest percent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339651/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a63a0ae-3e16-5cdb-92f5-fea09351db84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339651"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339650/selection/74051b9b97ebec6d2c02f9cdc6db086d2c8878e3b1e9a30d1096733aea305988" :answer/id #uuid "def1f97d-98d8-5fd6-ba37-12067a17517a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339650/selection/c2e823e227ba4c1a43ed78b128b1e9af689cb50a951bd5c91f505a2f99ab9421" :answer/id #uuid "e75504b9-4056-5892-91e5-591f76d38104" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339650/selection/f96c1746c3f5754c266cd46722fcf8c5048428430af7271ceb7c7ee57cd17750" :answer/id #uuid "8233c1c7-c945-5bd3-886c-9c3ade4ac6d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339650/selection/faaf82a36d334af25320fcede9baa3ca55fb45af5c9e6d640ea797e15c024dea" :answer/id #uuid "e1423694-056f-55e4-9ebc-61dc364a245a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339650/selection/a90f53dceeaaa2ca452b5d4e15ec3ca5ca035ec50c1e6a561c671f18b0222225" :answer/id #uuid "d7ac6e06-6630-5935-a6fe-c0095e4c7f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "46%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339650/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "62c28a90-1c61-50b6-9af9-07ce1b7459ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339650/selection/a90f53dceeaaa2ca452b5d4e15ec3ca5ca035ec50c1e6a561c671f18b0222225" :answer-field/choices ["q-339650/selection/74051b9b97ebec6d2c02f9cdc6db086d2c8878e3b1e9a30d1096733aea305988" "q-339650/selection/c2e823e227ba4c1a43ed78b128b1e9af689cb50a951bd5c91f505a2f99ab9421" "q-339650/selection/f96c1746c3f5754c266cd46722fcf8c5048428430af7271ceb7c7ee57cd17750" "q-339650/selection/faaf82a36d334af25320fcede9baa3ca55fb45af5c9e6d640ea797e15c024dea" "q-339650/selection/a90f53dceeaaa2ca452b5d4e15ec3ca5ca035ec50c1e6a561c671f18b0222225"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339650" :question/id #uuid "60b44c6a-0607-53dc-a99e-dce6dfb84419" :question/math-academy-id "q-339650" :question/problem "The population of a bacterial culture $N=N(t)$ after $t$ hours can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=kN,\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is the growth rate. If the culture initially contained $500$ bacteria, and $N(3)=2\\,000,$ calculate the growth rate $k$ to the nearest percent." :question/worked-solution "We model the population of the bacterial culture using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=kN.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nN(t)={N}_{0}\\,{e}^{kt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${N}_{0}$ is the initial population.\n\nWe're told that the culture initially contained $500$ bacteria, so we have ${N}_{0}=500.$\n\nTherefore, the population $N$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nN(t)=500\\,{e}^{kt}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $k,$ we substitute $N(3)=2\\,000$ into the equation above and solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(3) & =500\\,{e}^{k\\cdot 3} \\\\ 2\\,000 & =500\\,{e}^{3k} \\\\ {e}^{3k} & =\\frac{2\\,000}{500} \\\\ {e}^{3k} & =4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3k}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\ 3k & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\ k & =0.462\\,09…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k≈46%,$ rounded to the nearest percent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a63a0ae-3e16-5cdb-92f5-fea09351db84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119597/selection/a9f3019712710cffb301bd8f0c8e23a698096b2f757461b63171499fd4abd4af" :answer/id #uuid "0508390d-b2e8-5d2f-9bc2-6d2993161ef6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119597/selection/31ddfc2710d4ab7105ae7ca5a294aaeeeeec060271f0a446e6300752a06953d3" :answer/id #uuid "868615d9-0b84-5d22-ac2f-6ea9ef760a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119597/selection/3d7fd00e2f4c18a8838fa65513d89d267f397f8e45aab460a7fcbb008505a0ce" :answer/id #uuid "252e8e72-934c-5027-aae8-b120243cebc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119597/selection/3f12505bcd90a31098cdeba82adfc0f58c186e6b8641b13fcfc2cf221565263f" :answer/id #uuid "3a8a2d31-8f9a-588d-b0cf-6931f36dc212" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119597/selection/ba4e29521c6b503135428d16c5e65eb3dc46049b0808a13d1b984b5d9f70e4fb" :answer/id #uuid "a0f24df6-613d-5557-9ed8-5b16b51e8e5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119597/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "60f6cf4a-669d-5738-8caa-f91fb9caf015" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119597/selection/31ddfc2710d4ab7105ae7ca5a294aaeeeeec060271f0a446e6300752a06953d3" :answer-field/choices ["q-119597/selection/a9f3019712710cffb301bd8f0c8e23a698096b2f757461b63171499fd4abd4af" "q-119597/selection/31ddfc2710d4ab7105ae7ca5a294aaeeeeec060271f0a446e6300752a06953d3" "q-119597/selection/3d7fd00e2f4c18a8838fa65513d89d267f397f8e45aab460a7fcbb008505a0ce" "q-119597/selection/3f12505bcd90a31098cdeba82adfc0f58c186e6b8641b13fcfc2cf221565263f" "q-119597/selection/ba4e29521c6b503135428d16c5e65eb3dc46049b0808a13d1b984b5d9f70e4fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119597" :question/id #uuid "138cbf95-75f0-5bc8-9a00-62d7731a150b" :question/math-academy-id "q-119597" :question/problem "The value $V=V(t)$ of a certain art object $t$ years after its production can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is the growth rate. If it was initially worth $$2\\,000,$ and $V(10)=10\\,000$, calculate the value  of the growth rate $k$ to the nearest percent." :question/worked-solution "We model the value of the art object using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nV(t)={V}_{0}\\,{e}^{kt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${V}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that  it was initially worth $$2\\,000,$ so we have ${V}_{0}=2\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the value $V$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nV(t)=2\\,000\\,{e}^{kt}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $k,$ we substitute $V(10)=10\\,000$ into the equation above and solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(10) & =2\\,000\\,{e}^{k\\cdot 10} \\\\ 10\\,000 & =2\\,000\\,{e}^{10k} \\\\ {e}^{10k} & =\\frac{10\\,000}{2\\,000} \\\\ {e}^{10k} & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{10k}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ 10k & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ k & ≈0.16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k≈16%,$ rounded to the nearest percent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119597/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a63a0ae-3e16-5cdb-92f5-fea09351db84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119597"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353211/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "491d6765-3d5b-5d12-b6d8-b4cf977d8a21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353211/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d34997d2-ca19-5a30-9dbd-8e2edb24363b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353211/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-353211/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353211" :question/id #uuid "7761cbe4-947b-53e4-a7fb-0a91fd60ca66" :question/math-academy-id "q-353211" :question/problem "The number of subscribers $S=S(t)$ to a website $t$ months after a marketing campaign can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=kS\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is the growth rate. If there were $12\\,000$ subscribers initially, and $S(2)=15\\,000$, calculate the value of the growth rate $k$ to the nearest percent.\n\n$k≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$%$" :question/worked-solution "We model the number of subscribers using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=kS.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nS(t)={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{kt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there were $12\\,000$ subscribers initially, so we have ${S}_{0}=12\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the number of subscribers $S$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nS(t)=12\\,000\\,{e}^{kt}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $k,$ we substitute $S(2)=15\\,000$ into the equation above and solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(2) & =12\\,000\\,{e}^{k\\cdot 2} \\\\ 15\\,000 & =12\\,000\\,{e}^{2k} \\\\ {e}^{2k} & =\\frac{15\\,000}{12\\,000} \\\\ {e}^{2k} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2k}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\ 2k & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\ k & ≈0.111\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k≈11%,$ rounded to the nearest percent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353211/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a63a0ae-3e16-5cdb-92f5-fea09351db84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353211"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353210/field-1/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "90825270-d1f0-5c68-8f79-8569e4c0ef00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353210/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3129585-ac30-5a70-88b4-dbe8f87c825d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353210/field-1/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-353210/field-1/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353210" :question/id #uuid "0c08f0b2-a661-5e5b-99bf-b3525675c872" :question/math-academy-id "q-353210" :question/problem "The number of bacteria $N=N(t)$ in a laboratory culture $t$ hours after observation can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=kN\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is the growth rate. If there were $500$ bacteria initially, and $N(3)=900$, calculate the value of the growth rate $k$ to the nearest percent.\n\n$k≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$%$" :question/worked-solution "We model the number of bacteria using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=kN.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nN(t)={N}_{0}\\,{e}^{kt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${N}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there were $500$ bacteria initially, so we have ${N}_{0}=500.$\n\nTherefore, the number of bacteria $N$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nN(t)=500\\,{e}^{kt}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $k,$ we substitute $N(3)=900$ into the equation above and solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(3) & =500\\,{e}^{k\\cdot 3} \\\\ 900 & =500\\,{e}^{3k} \\\\ {e}^{3k} & =\\frac{900}{500} \\\\ {e}^{3k} & =\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3k}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{5}) \\\\ 3k & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{5}) \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{5}) \\\\ k & ≈0.1959\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k≈20%,$ rounded to the nearest percent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353210/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a63a0ae-3e16-5cdb-92f5-fea09351db84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-542"] :question/problem "Suppose that the population $P(t)$ of a town after $t$ years can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}P} {\\textrm{d}t} = 0.02P.\n$$\n\nIf there are currently $500$ people in the town, what will be the town's population in $3$ years?" :question/worked-solution "We note that this is an exponential growth differential equation with $r = 0.02$. Therefore, the solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t) = P_0\\,e^{0.02t},\n$$\n\nwhere $P_0$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that the population is currently $500,$ so we have $P_0 = 500.$ \n\nTherefore, the population of the town at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nP(t) = 500\\,e^{0.02t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the population after $3$ years, we substitute $t=3$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3) & =500\\,{e}^{0.02\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =500\\,{e}^{0.06} \\\\  & ≈531\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the population will be approximately $531$ after $3$ years." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7312"] :question/problem "Suppose that the value $V(t)$ of a particular car can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t} = -0.1V,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the car was first purchased. If the car was purchased for $\\[math]10\\,000,$ what will it be worth after $3$ years?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the right-hand side of the equation is *negative*, which means that the car's value is *decreasing.*\n\nThis is an exponential decay differential equation with $r = 0.1.$ Therefore, the general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nV(t) = V_0 e^{-0.1 t}.\n$$\n\nWe know that the car was first purchased for $\\[math]10\\,000.$ Therefore, $V_0 = 10\\,000,$ and we have the particular solution\n\n$$\nV(t) = 10\\,000 e^{-0.1 t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the car's value after $3$ years, we substitute $t=3$ into the particular solution above. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(3) & =10\\,000{e}^{-0.1\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =10\\,000{e}^{-0.3} \\\\  & ≈7\\,408.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the car will be worth approximately $\\[/math]7\\,408$ after three years." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7273"] :question/worked-solution "The rate $N'(t)$ at which the number of followers increases is directly proportional to the number of followers $N.$ Therefore, we can model the number of followers using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d} N}{\\mathrm{d} t} = rN,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is measured in months, and $r > 0$ is the growth rate.\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nN(t) = N_0\\,e^{rt},\n$$\n\nwhere $N_0$ is the initial number of followers.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $600\\,000$ followers, so we have $N_0 = 600\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the number of followers $N$ after $t$ months is\n\n$$\nN(t) = 600\\,000 \\, e^{rt} .\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the growth rate, we substitute $N(3)=780\\,000$ into the equation above and solve for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(3) & =600\\,000\\,{e}^{r\\cdot 3} \\\\ 780\\,000 & =600\\,000\\,{e}^{3r} \\\\ {e}^{3r} & =\\frac{780\\,000}{600\\,000} \\\\ {e}^{3r} & =1.3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.3) \\\\ 3r & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.3) \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.3) \\\\ r & ≈0.087\\,54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $r\\approx 9\\%,$ rounded to the nearest percent." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
